{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14268 - PROTEIN:3781",
  "verbalization": "Benzocaine is implicated in a complex network of interactions leading to the activation of C-C chemokine receptor type 2. The evidence suggests that benzocaine acts as a target for a common intermediate, 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline, which in turn targets the C-C chemokine receptor type 2. This pathway is supported by multiple independent connections, with benzocaine directly targeting the tumor susceptibility gene 101 protein, which is also a target of the quinoline compound. The shared involvement of 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline in targeting both the tumor susceptibility gene 101 protein and the C-C chemokine receptor type 2 indicates a potential mechanistic link through this quinoline compound. The presence of multiple overlapping targets and the consistent involvement of the quinoline compound in this chain of interactions strongly supports the hypothesis that benzocaine indirectly influences C-C chemokine receptor type 2 through this intermediate.",
